1. `tLocal` is a `const` (line 5340) — it's captured once from the original keyframe position
2. On every `pointermove`, it calls `moveKeyframeForSelectedClip(kfData.paramId, tLocal, clampedTMs, clampedValue)` where `tLocal` is ALWAYS the original position
3. After the first move, the old keyframe at `tLocal` (original position) is gone — it was moved to `clampedTMs`
4. On the second `pointermove`, it tries to remove from `tLocal` (original position) which no longer exists, so it doesn't find it and ADDS a new one
